# SPOTS development invariants

- **Toolchain:** use the Node version in [.nvmrc](mdc:spots-app/.nvmrc); `npm install` / `npm run dev` / `npm run build`; ESLint + Prettier.
- **TypeScript:** new code in TypeScript only; concise functional style (prefer functions over classes); names like `isLoading` / `hasError`; early returns for errors and edge cases.
- **Structure:** put business logic in hooks and services under `app/_lib/` (not only in UI). Prefer composition and shared validation over copy-paste.
- **REDCap (development):** no mock or silent fallbacks. All data must come from REDCap-backed APIs; if data is unavailable, fail explicitly so broken integration is obvious.
- **Security:** never commit secrets (use `.env`); validate inputs on the server; sanitize/escape outputs; least-privilege auth.
- **App UI/code patterns** (App Router, Tailwind, typing): follow `app-patterns` when editing `app/`.
- **Amplify / Cognito backend:** follow `amplify-backend` when touching `amplify/` or auth services.
- **SpotSymptoms:** reference-only — never modify (see `Do-not-modify`).
